    "result_text": "There's a single test class and it passes. The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans, while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern (each derived Owner field is a small cohesive helper referenced by a MapStruct expression), I made three low-impact changes:\n\n1. **New helper `mapper/TelephoneDisplays.java`** \u2014 a small self-contained class (WMC_other = 0) with one static `format` method that splits the country code (`+61`/`+1`) and groups the national digits in threes, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on the existing `toOwnerDto` method (an abstract method with CC 1 in a small interface), mirroring the `displayName`/`ageBand`/etc. expressions.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the generated `Owner` schema so the DTO exposes it.\n\nNo existing method was grown and nothing was added to a large class. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`.",
